  "id": "DrugBank_DB01039 - MONDO_5347",
  "verbalization": "Fenofibrate is implicated in the pathogenesis of Hypertriglyceridemia (disease) through a series of interconnected pharmacological relationships. The evidence suggests that Fenofibrate, through its indication for Hyperlipidemia, Familial Combined, Lpl Related, and its association with Pravastatin, which in turn indicates Hypertriglyceridemia, may exert a role in lipid metabolism. This is further supported by its indication for Hypoalphalipoproteinemia, which links to Simvastatin, another drug that is known to influence lipid levels and potentially contribute to hypertriglyceridemia. The presence of multiple pathways involving lipid-lowering agents, such as Fenofibrate, Pravastatin, and Simvastatin, indicates a potential mechanism by which these drugs may influence triglyceride levels. The integration of these relationships highlights the role of lipid-lowering medications in the development of hypertriglyceridemia, though the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated.",
